target:    src/Migration/Migrations/AddUserAgentDimension.php
gate:      php tests/schema-single-source-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    ALTER TABLE statement(s) outside
rationale: Column DDL written by hand again, and deliberately WITHOUT the optional COLUMN keyword. MySQL's grammar is `ADD [COLUMN]`, so `ALTER TABLE t ADD ua_id BINARY(8)` is valid and one word shorter than what shipped — and the first draft of this gate, which enumerated `(?:ADD|MODIFY|CHANGE)\s+COLUMN`, was blind to exactly this form. That is why the scan keys on `ALTER TABLE`, which has no optional spelling. This mutation is the only thing standing between the gate and a return to keyword enumeration.
---
--- a/src/Migration/Migrations/AddUserAgentDimension.php
+++ b/src/Migration/Migrations/AddUserAgentDimension.php
@@ -122,6 +122,7 @@
         // Two literal calls, not a loop, for the same reason AddVisitIdentity gives: the
         // schema-single-source gate resolves LITERAL (table, column) arguments against the
         // manifest, and a variable table name is a call site that gate cannot see.
+        $this->wpdb->query('ALTER TABLE ' . $this->tablePrefix() . 'slim_stats ADD ua_id BINARY(8) NULL');
         $ok = $this->addManifestColumn('slim_stats', 'ua_id', 'add_user_agent_dimension')
             && $this->addManifestColumn('slim_stats_archive', 'ua_id', 'add_user_agent_dimension');
 
